    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432">

                <pb facs="0599" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.1121 Hrinkevich, Frank/2: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davies</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1937-10-21T14:00:00+03:00">October 21, 1937—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 21—9:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>274. Embassy’s telegram 268, October 18, 11 a.m. Foreign Office stated orally
                    today at 1:00 p.m., that Durbrow, who is en route from Berlin and will arrive
                    this evening in Minsk, may not interview Hrinkevich.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Davies</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
